  "question": {
    "text": "Temperature of an ideal gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The final temperature of the gas when its volume changes from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> in the process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>αV</mi></math> (here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></math> is a positive constant) is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>900</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1200</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "The given relation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>∝</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math><br /><br />Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>∝</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math><br /><br />When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> changes from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> is also doubled<br /><br />For an ideal gas, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>pV</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo></math>constant<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>∝</mo><mi>pV</mi></math>. Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> becomes <math><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> times<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>300</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1200</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>"
  }
